# Dense extensions for weighted restricted spherical maximal estimates

The strong-type estimates used in the power-weight argument are first proved
on Schwartz functions.  This file records the standard, representative-safe
way to pass such an estimate to all `L^p` classes.  The extension is an
`Lp`-valued operator: for arbitrary equivalence classes it would be wrong to
claim that a pointwise spherical average is canonically defined.

The abstract lemma is stated for a measure for which Schwartz functions are a
dense core.  The specialization below applies it to the power-weight measure
once its usual local-finiteness hypotheses have been established.
